From a91e22377f9e42b6daecc719ab1cf355b49c12e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baptiste Pignier <pignier.baptiste@tutanota.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:27:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] goodixtls53xd: Calibrate the background and improve
 captures

- With the OTP DAC values the finger-free sensor saturates at 4095, so the
  background subtraction removed a constant and the fixed pattern of the
  sensor stayed in every image, where SIGFM matched it across fingers.
  The DAC shifts every pixel linearly (~73 per step): take finger-free
  frames at DAC +20 and +40, extrapolate the background at the finger DAC,
  and detect the finger at +20 against the matching frame.
- Wait for the contact delta to settle before capturing, and ask for a
  retry when the finger is lifted early or the contact is too light.
- Enroll 20 images, each one only covers a small part of the finger.
- Use a SIGFM threshold of 10: impostors never scored above 3 offline.
- Disable the temperature model like goodixmoc: polling images for the
  finger exhausted it during a collection session.
- Retry the activation when a command times out: the reader is runtime
  suspended after 2 s idle and the first command after resuming may be
  lost. Also report TLS activation errors instead of never completing.
- Debug dumps ($GOODIX53XD_DUMP_DIR) of raw frames, calibration frames,
  final image and contact delta per press, and $GOODIX53XD_DAC_OFFSET and
  $GOODIX53XD_MIN_CONTACT to explore settings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libfprint/drivers/goodixtls/goodix53xd.c | 343 ++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 301 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libfprint/drivers/goodixtls/goodix53xd.c b/libfprint/drivers/goodixtls/goodix53xd.c
